!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = experiment: NMD screen
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = lentiviral library received: Brunello library
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = reporter cell line: NMD reporter
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = N/A.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Fluorescent-reporter coupled CRISPR/Cas9-mediated loss of function screening was carried out as described in Golden et al., Nature, 2017, except for the Brunello library (Addgene #73179) but not the GeCKO V2 libarary was used, in both NMD EGFP reporter and control EGFP reporter cell lines. Reporter cell line generation and more information about the screen are described in the manuscript.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was extracted from cell pellets using either a gDNA isolation method that has been previously described Golden et al., Nature, 2017 for the sorted cells or the MasterPureTM Complete DNA Purification Kit (Lucigen) for the unsorted cells.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = PCR amplicon libraries were generated as described in the manuscript.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = CRISPR/Cas9-mediated loss of function screening.
!Sample_description = sgRNA sequence amplified out of genomic DNA
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were mapped to Brunello library sgRNA reference files.
!Sample_data_processing = Normalized read counts were calculated as described in Shalem et al., Science, 2014.
!Sample_data_processing = MAGeCK (Li et al., Genome Biology, 2014) was used to assign significance to each gene targeted by the sgRNAs in the Brunello library.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: Brunello library sgRNA reference files obtained from Addgene
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: A table of normalized read counts for each sgRNA in each sample is provided.
